:"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/27237246812/27237246812_e5a584eb15_o.jpg","sha256":"0d2192273b37a443f6fb1a2926f5420946b04969b909125d8b9ea49ec99b122b","tags":["bike","tour","sooke","sooke potholes","bc","canada"],"taken":"2016-04-17 08:50:44","title":"IMG_3400","uploaded":"2016-05-29 13:01:38","width":2888},"27243047895":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":5848},{"id":"72157668686880006","position":27}],"bytes":2877091,"camera_position":5848,"comments":[{"author":"88645634@N07","date":"2016-05-25 12:29:14","text":"Is this on the Galloping Goose headed towards Sooke?"},{"author":"26941526@N00","date":"2016-05-25 23:25:26","text":"Yup!\nwww.sookenewsmirror.com/opinion/323685501.html \nen.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay-class_minesweeper"},{"author":"88645634@N07","date":"2016-05-26 00:35:29","text":"[https://www.flickr.com/photos/26941526@N00] www.flickr.com/photos/pedalpusher61/20850633628/in/album-..."}],"description":"Riding on the Galloping Goose wit @rhymeswithbombs","detail":"photos/0098.json","filename":"27243047895_253df1fd6f_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/27243047895/","height":2090,"id":"27243047895","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/27243047895/27243047895_253df1fd6f_o.jpg","sha256":"99e38dda3acc8a13426483949e16eb1a1e6768e7e0d314c21ee7f669542a7b32","tags":["bike","bicycles","sooke","galloping goose trail","bc","canada"],"taken":"2016-04-16 14:19:28","title":"IMG_3172","uploaded":"2016-05-25 07:47:53","width":3853},"27243052315":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":5847},{"id":"72157668686880006","position":26}],"bytes":5882370,"camera_position":5847,"comments":[],"description":"Riding on the Galloping Goose wit @rhymeswithbombs","detail":"photos/0098.json","filename":"27243052315_8c48a667a5_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/27243052315/","height":4000,"id":"27243052315","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/27243052315/27243052315_8c48a667a5_o.jpg","sha256":"b631ffd34c3d1792ff975cca92b0633fea8b55b5aebf8725ba8dfe923b8f2cc3","tags":["bike","bicycles","sooke","galloping goose trail","bc","canada"],"taken":"2016-04-16 13:37:41","title":"IMG_3168","uploaded":"2016-05-25 07:48:04","width":3000},"27243058105":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":5845},{"id":"72157668686880006","position":24}],"bytes":4786127,"camera_position":5845,"comments":[{"author":"50167308@N06","date":"2016-05-25 11:30:34","text":"Totally my kind of bike ..."},{"author":"118932233@N04","date":"2016-05-25 13:00:20","text":"..reminds me my solo-tour \n1 Year New Zealand \nround North and  South Island each..\nhiking several times up to  Mount Cook . . \nthen\n..crossing Stewart Island (somehow ..there are only a few lanes)..\nand after that Australia . . ."},{"author":"100330886@N04","date":"2016-05-26 06:14:46","text":"@rhymeswithbombs did a nice job putting this bike together.  @*\u1548\u15e9\u1570\u14aa  that sounds like a lot of nice riding."},{"author":"50167308@N06","date":"2016-05-28 01:58:27","text":"The fork is not the original one - but I've found the related story to this in the meantime. Maybe some day a better fork comes across ...\nHere in Germany one can have a t-casted lugged fork from Surly for around $90-100. Not sure if this is an alternative."},{"author":"100330886@N04","date":"2016-05-31 07:04:13","text":"@rhymeswithbombs has a number of beautiful frankenstein bikes.  I don't remember where this fork was from, maybe he could chime in."},{"author":"26941526@N00","date":"2016-06-07 16:41:14","text":"[https://www.flickr.com/photos/italobikes-v2jo]  [https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering] \nThis fork is the second attempt at replacing the sadly mangled original.\nMy requirements were that it fit a wider 700C tire than a real \"roadie\" fork, and ideally fenders, and have brake posts. The selection of used forks locally that fit that description is limited. I think this one cost $10 or $15. The whole bike came to less than $100, so I wouldn't spend that much on a fork. I didn't want a unicrown fork, but beggars can't be choosers.\n\nI've since scored a really nice lugged Nishiki touring fork (complete with headset) with double drop-out eyelets and even midfork braze-ons for $35, but I haven't swapped it out yet because I'll have to have about an inch of new threads cut into the steerer tube and a couple inches cut off the top. Maybe later this summer....\n\nIn the meantime, I'm VERY happy with how it has turned out!"}],"description":"Riding on the Galloping Goose wit @rhymeswithbombs","detail":"photos/0098.json","filename":"27243058105_bb8e305a70_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/27243058105/","height":2150,"id":"27243058105","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/27243058105/27243058105_bb8e305a70_o.jpg","sha256":"25f5813ac80bc4e3c89d8df44cf13dbe6c925fdb4e5f698cb55d8471cf9bd16e","tags":["bike","bicycles","sooke","galloping goose trail","bc","canada"],"taken":"2016-04-16 13:15:23","title":"IMG_3159","uploaded":"2016-05-25 07:48:17","width":3950},"27243063035":{"albums":[{"id":"72157643911711523","position":5843},{"id":"72157668686880006","position":22}],"bytes":4328571,"camera_position":5843,"comments":[{"author":"127508165@N06","date":"2016-05-25 09:22:37","text":"Always great to see that red-green contrast :-)"}],"description":"Riding on the Galloping Goose wit @rhymeswithbombs","detail":"photos/0098.json","filename":"27243063035_da936f365d_o.jpg","flickr_url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/earthwandering/27243063035/","height":2588,"id":"27243063035","kind":"photo","license":"All Rights Reserved","original":"originals/27243063035/27243063035_da936f365d_o.jpg","sha256":"d142df09f8d07213b9677881d6e0cd129a23fc9013bfbd2b345042637a6a8d37","tags":["bike","bicycles","sooke","galloping goose trail","bc","canada"],"taken":"2016-04-16 12:52:47","title":"IMG_3150","uploade